# Singe's Lua parses these files byte by byte and slices fields with string.sub,
# so a CR is not whitespace to it — it lands inside the last field on the line.
# readScore takes a level's difficulty letter as everything after '!', which
# makes a CRLF file yield "E\r" where every comparison expects "E".
#
# core.autocrlf is on for this repo, so without these rules a fresh clone on
# Windows checks them out as CRLF and ships them that way.
*.cfg    text eol=lf
*.singe  text eol=lf

# Source is stored LF. Nothing reads a CR here, but a checkout that flips a few
# files to CRLF rewrites every line of them in the next diff, which buries the
# real change - and it has happened twice, both times after a rebase.
*.cs     text eol=lf
*.axaml  text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
